  "Canon has {name}’s hair as {word}.": "",
  "Canon keeps the facts of your world (who is a mare, whose eyes are grey, how the town is spelt), each one tied to the line that says it. When a later line disagrees, it tells you quietly, once you stop typing. It never writes a word for you, and it runs on this computer.": "",
  "Canon keeps track of who and what is in this world, from every book on the shelf.": "",
  "Canon keeps your world’s facts, each one citing the passage it came from, and when a later line disagrees (a mare who is “he” in chapter two), it tells you quietly, once you stop typing. You write; it never writes for you, and it runs on this computer, offline.": "",
  "Canon leaves this out. Nothing in it is a fact, and nothing in it is checked.": "",
  "Canon needs a reader": "",
  "Canon needs the reader to keep the story’s key points.": "",
  "Canon Reader": "",
  "Canon Reader…": "",
  "Canon reads every book and notebook on this shelf, and only what changed since it last read. Facts you wrote or confirmed are never changed.": "",
  "Canon reads your books and notes and keeps track of who and what is in your world — every fact tied to the line that says it. The reader runs on this computer. Nothing you write is sent anywhere.": "",
  "Canon stopped reading. What it read is kept; Read the Shelf carries on from there.": "",
  "Canon treats every book on this shelf as one world, and books added here later join it. A story of its own can have a shelf of its own.": "",
  "Canon treats every book on this shelf as one world. If this book is its own story, move it to a shelf of its own first.": "",
  "Canon will find every passage that says otherwise and show you each change. Nothing changes until you apply it.": "",
  "Canon will flag this line again on the next pass.": "",
